##### Discord

##### Building the Discord Tracks

> **BUILDING TENSION**
>
> Creating satisfying discord doesn’t mean “trapping” your PCs in an unsolvable problem where one has to “defeat” the other. Conflicts between characters are often best when they are a matter of give and take, with each character winning on some accounts and losing on others. Alternately, you can prepare a common enemy—perhaps underlying cause of both complications—who the PCs can rally against at the end, diffusing the tension.

##### Choosing a Session’s Discord

#### Awarding XP

#### Character Death and Retirement

> **BUSHIDŌ IN HISTORICAL JAPAN**
>
> Rokugani Bushidō is quite different from anything that existed historically in Japan. While historical samurai had deeply held convictions that they lived and died for, there is no single text that defined Bushidō for all samurai.
>
> Outside of Japan, cultural understanding of Bushidō comes in large part from retrospective efforts to understand the past. Inazo Nitobe’s Bushido: The Soul of Japan (1900) is one text written by a Japanese scholar to explain Bushidō to English speakers. Nitobe offers “Military-Knight-Ways” as a translation of Bushidō, and expands it to the “‘Precepts of Knighthood,’ the noblesse oblige of the warrior class.”
>
> Much as the code of chivalry in Europe has been romanticized to fit with the values of later writers, Nitobe’s account of Bushidō is a product of its own time (after the era of samurai), and it can help readers understand the history of Western views on Bushidō.

### Using Social Attributes

#### Honor in Play

##### Forfeiting and Staking Honor

##### Awarding Honor for Deeds

