| Trifling | 1 | 1 |
| Minor | Attribute Rank | 3 |
| Major | Attribute Rank x 2 | 6 |
| Massive | Attribute Rank x 4 | 9 |

> **The Clans’ Views of Bushidō**
>
> Each clan has one or more tenets it views as paramount, even above the others. When a character chooses to forfeit honor due to defying one of their own clan’s paramount tenets, they double the amount of honor they must forfeit. When a character is awarded honor as a result of making a personal sacrifice for this tenet, the GM should double the honor they are awarded.
>
> - Crab: Courage
> - Crane: Courtesy
> - Dragon: Sincerity
> - Lion: Honor
> - Phoenix: Righteousness
> - Scorpion: Duty and Loyalty
> - Unicorn: Compassion Each clan has one or more tenets of Bushidō it views as less significant than the others. When a character chooses to forfeit honor due to defy this tenet, halve the amount of honor they must forfeit (rounded up, to a minimum of 1). When a character is awarded honor for making a personal sacrifice in the name of this tenet, halve the honor they are awarded (rounded up, to a minimum of 1).
> - Crab: Courtesy
> - Crane: Courage
> - Dragon: Duty and Loyalty
> - Lion: Compassion
> - Phoenix: Sincerity
> - Scorpion: Honor and Righteousness
> - Unicorn: Courtesy

> **BUSHIDŌ IN ROKUGAN**
>
> Within the fictional world of Rokugan, honor is believed to be more objective than it is subjective. The Rokugani code of honor does vary somewhat in interpretation, but samurai mostly agree on what the perfect samurai should believe, live for, and die for. It is a harsh code, and it values some lives above others.
>
> Unlike in historical Japan, the bulk of Rokugani Bushidō’s demands are spelled out in a single text—Akodo’s Leadership. There is little room for shades of gray, and even those samurai who do not hold themselves to every demand of Bushidō generally believe in the code’s value. Where they disagree is on which tenets of Bushidō can be allowed to slide with the least consequence, and which must be upheld no matter what.

#### The Tenets of Bushidō

##### Breaches of Compassion

