##### Breaches of Courage

> **SCORPION HONOR**
>
> The Scorpion Clan is particularly illustrative of the perceived objectivity of honor: its members do not debate the definitions of honor or attempt to rationalize their actions as honorable through twisted logic, but they also do not believe that honor is worthless. They accept that members of Bayushi’s clan cannot behave according to Bushidō precepts, but they do not actually disagree with what these precepts are or even that they are valuable. Honor is for other samurai, and they can be honorable only because the Scorpion are willing to do the dirty work that a society demands.

> **REWARDS IN DEATH**
>
> There is another reason why a samurai is so willing to live dangerously. The concept of loyalty goes both ways. A daimyō will be loyal to a fallen samurai’s memory by rewarding their family in return for their devotion.

